          "width": 257,
          "height": 387
        },
        "pageimage": "SingularitySky(1stEd).jpg",
        "extract": "Singularity Sky is a science fiction novel by British writer Charles Stross, published in 2003. A sequel, Iron Sunrise, was published that same year. Together the two are referred to as the Eschaton novels, after a near-godlike intelligence that exists in both.\nThe novel follows the ill-fated military campaign by a repressive state, the New Republic, to retaliate for a perceived invasion of one of its colony worlds. In actuality, the planet has been visited by the Festival, a technologically advanced alien or posthuman race that rewards its hosts for \"entertaining\" them by granting whatever the entertainer wishes, including the Festival's own...",
